    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i just realized i dont even know what i like anymore. like, if i go to the store, i just stand in the aisle staring at stuff because nothing feels like \"mine\". everything i did for ten years was for us. now the apartment is just too quiet and i feel like im just walking around as a ghost. i dont even feel like a real person anymore.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a very heavy realization, and it's completely understandable that you feel lost when your entire focus was on someone else. That feeling of being a ghost is a sign that you're finally free to let yourself be, but you don't have to figure out \"what you like\" right now. Sometimes the only thing that feels right is the quiet, simple act of letting yourself just *be* in the stillness.",
      "source": "target",
